---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RelatedWorkflows from '../../components/RelatedWorkflows.astro';
import Screenshot from '../../components/Screenshot.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Workflows', url: '/workflows' },
  { name: 'Client Portal', url: '/workflows/client-portal' }
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What can clients see in the portal?',
    answer: 'You control what\'s visible. Clients can access pedigrees, health records, photos, contracts, payment history, and messages, based on permissions you set.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can clients make payments through the portal?',
    answer: 'Yes, when you accept card payments. Clients see their invoices, payment history, and balance, and pay from the invoice on a secure Stripe Checkout page. If you collect another way, the invoice shows your payment instructions instead.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do clients need to download an app?',
    answer: 'No. The portal is web-based and works on any device with a browser. Access is by your invitation: the buyer opens the activation link in their email, sets a password, and signs in.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How does a buyer get into the portal?',
    answer: 'Only because you gave them access. You can enable access from a contact or from a waitlist entry, and BreederHQ also sets it up when you send go-home documents, a pickup window invitation, an invoice, or a buyer selection turn. The buyer gets a Your Client Portal is Ready email with an activation link. Access you suspended or removed stays off.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can buyers book their own go-home time?',
    answer: 'It is your choice per booking window. Buyers can pick an open time themselves and change or cancel it within your cutoffs, or you can schedule every buyer yourself. Buyers in a window you schedule see their time and can add it to a calendar, but they cannot book, change, or cancel it.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I message clients through the portal?',
    answer: 'Yes. Built-in messaging keeps all communication in one place. Clients receive notifications when you send updates.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Is client data secure?',
    answer: 'Yes. Each client has their own secure login and can only see information about their own animals and transactions. All data is encrypted.'
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Client Portal, Built for Breeders | BreederHQ"
  description="Give buyers secure 24/7 access to their animal’s pedigree, health records, photos, and contracts, cutting repeat requests. See the client portal."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <a href="#main-content" class="skip-link sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-50 focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:bg-white focus:text-black focus:shadow-lg focus:rounded">
    Skip to content
  </a>

  <main id="main-content">
  <nav class="breadcrumb py-4 px-4 bg-gray-50" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol class="flex items-center space-x-2 max-w-4xl mx-auto text-sm">
      <li><a href="/" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">Home</a></li>
      <li class="text-gray-400">›</li>
      <li><a href="/workflows" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">Workflows</a></li>
      <li class="text-gray-400">›</li>
      <li aria-current="page" class="text-gray-600">Client Portal</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <!-- Section 1: What This Page Is About -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold mb-6">A Client Portal, Built for Breeders.</h1>

      <aside class="tldr-box bg-gray-100 border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] p-6 my-8 rounded" role="complementary" aria-label="Page summary">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Quick Summary</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          Give every buyer a secure portal where they can see their animal's pedigree, health records, photos, contracts, payment history, and messages, any time, from any device. You control what is visible, and routine questions are answered before they even come up.
        </p>
      </aside>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        You already send buyers pedigrees, health records, photos, and payment reminders. A client portal keeps all of that in one secure place so buyers can find what they need on their own, whenever they need it, while you focus on the animals.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12">
        <Screenshot
          id="portal-buyer-home"
          alt="Buyer portal home view in BreederHQ branded as Cedar Ridge Kennels"
        />
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-3 text-center italic">
          Every buyer gets a portal branded as your kennel, with their animal, documents, payments, and messages all in one place.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Why Breeders Search for This -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">You already answer these questions. A portal just answers them for you.</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        These are the requests that fill up every breeder's week:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>"Can you send the health records again?" and you dig through files</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>"What's my remaining balance?" and you check your records</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>"Do you have photos from last week?" and you search your phone</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>"Where's my contract?" and you hunt through email</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>"Any updates on my animal?" and you type out the same status to each buyer, whether it's a puppy, kitten, foal, kid, lamb, or kit</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>Clients wait for you to respond before they can access anything</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        These interruptions add up. A client portal handles most of them automatically, so your time stays focused on the animals.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: How Breeders Usually Handle It -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">The tools you've been using</h2>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Email attachments</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            You send documents, photos, and updates via email. Clients lose them and ask again. You re-send. Repeat.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Text messages</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Quick updates go through text. Photos get buried in the conversation. Finding that specific photo from three weeks ago takes a lot of scrolling.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Social media groups</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Some breeders create Facebook groups to share updates on litters, foals, kids, lambs, kits, or calves. Great for photos, but not a great home for contracts, payments, or private information.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Dropbox or Google Drive folders</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Shared folders for documents. Better than email for files, but no messaging, no payments, no structure. Clients can view files but cannot interact.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Manual responses to every request</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            The most common approach is to personally answer every question. It works, until the volume catches up with you.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: Where That Breaks Down -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">Where those tools start to stretch thin</h2>

      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">You're always the first point of contact</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            A buyer needs something at 9pm and messages you. Because there is no self-service option, the default is to interrupt you, even for things as simple as pulling up a pedigree.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Information gets lost</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            You sent the pedigree three times and the buyer still cannot find it. Email and text threads are not designed for document access, so even attentive buyers lose track.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Payment tracking gets awkward</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            "What's my balance?" shouldn't require a conversation every time. Without a portal, you are manually calculating and communicating payment status for each buyer.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Communication is scattered across platforms</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Some clients text, some email, some message on social media. You are checking multiple platforms constantly, and important messages can slip through.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">The experience doesn't match the price</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Buyers investing thousands of dollars expect a professional experience from start to finish. A dedicated portal matches the quality of the animals you are placing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">More clients, more juggling</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Five clients are manageable with texts and emails. Fifteen is a lot to hold together. Your program grows, and your communication tools need to grow with it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 5: What a Correct System Looks Like -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">What it looks like when everything is connected</h2>

      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Document access</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Contracts viewable and downloadable anytime</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Health records, vaccination certificates, medication history, registration papers</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Pedigree documents</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Any document you choose to share</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Contracts & E-Signatures</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Buyers sign the contracts you send them in the portal, and you countersign. You can upload the PDF contract you already use, or build merge-field templates that pull from your records. See <a href="/workflows/contracts-and-e-signatures" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">Contracts & E-Signatures</a> for how it works.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Photo and update access</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Photos organized by date, not buried in messages</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Growth updates, weight tracking, milestone photos</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Clients can view anytime without asking</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Notifications when new content is added</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Payment visibility</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Payment history visible to client</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Outstanding balance clearly displayed</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Pay online by card from the invoice, when you accept card payments</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Payment instructions on the invoice when you collect another way, such as check or bank transfer</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>A downloadable PDF copy of every invoice</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Centralized messaging</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>All communication in one thread</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Message history preserved</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Notifications for both parties</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>No more hunting across email/text/social</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Secure, individual access</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Each client has their own login</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Only sees their animals and information</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>You control what's visible per client</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Professional, branded experience</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 5.1: Portal Access -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">How Buyers Get Into Your Portal</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        The portal is invitation-only. A buyer reaches it because you gave them access, not by signing up on a public site.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">You Control the Invitation</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Manage access from a contact's Portal tab, or from the Portal tab in a waitlist entry. Both show the same status: no access yet, invited, active, or suspended.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Enable Access sends the invite, Resend Invite sends it again, and Suspend Access cuts off the portal. Re-enable Access restores it.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>If a buyer is locked out, Send Password Reset Link emails them a link to set a new one.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Access you suspended or removed stays off. Nobody can claim it by signing in.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">What the Buyer Does</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Opens the Your Client Portal is Ready email, sets a password or signs in with an existing BreederHQ account, accepts the Terms, and lands in the portal.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>If an invitation link has expired, the buyer does not need a new one. They sign in or create an account with the email address you have on file and accept the invitation on the next page.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>BreederHQ also sets up access when you send go-home documents, a pickup window invitation, an invoice, or a buyer selection turn. A new buyer may then receive two emails: yours, and the portal-ready email. Reminders and receipts never grant access on their own.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Know Whether the Invite Landed</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>A delivery badge shows whether the invite email was delivered, bounced, or failed.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>A bounced invite adds a warning next to the contact's email in the contacts list and sends you an in-app notification, so you can correct the address and send again.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>If a buyer has no email on file, or their communication preferences block portal email, the tab tells you why the invite actions are unavailable.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>If the connection drops mid-send, the tab holds the invite buttons until it can read the current status, so you never send a second invitation blindly.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 5.2: Go-Home Scheduling -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">Go-Home Scheduling in the Portal</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        A booking window is one offer of go-home times, such as a weekend of pickups, for the buyers on a breeding plan. You decide who books, you can place any buyer yourself, and you control the emails buyers receive.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Choose Who Books</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Buyers Book Their Own Time: buyers pick an open time in the portal and can change or cancel it until your cutoffs. If it is not their turn yet, the page shows when it opens.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>I Schedule Every Buyer: you give each buyer a time. They see it and can add it to a calendar, but they cannot book, change, or cancel it, and are told to contact you to change it.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Add, move, or cancel a buyer's time yourself at any time. The buyer is emailed the change, and that email always sends.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">See Who Is Coming, and When</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>The Scheduling section of a breeding plan shows every time in each window and who holds it, with a count such as 6 of 10 booked.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Booked Only hides open times so you see just who is coming. Buyers who have not booked are listed by name so you can place them.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>You can take one day out of a window and keep the rest. A day that still has bookings cannot be removed until you move or cancel them, so no buyer loses a time without you choosing it.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Buyer emails show times in your saved business time zone, with the zone named, so a buyer in another zone knows exactly when to arrive.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">What Your Buyers Receive</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Three switches in Settings apply to every window: a window-open invite, one reminder to a buyer who has not booked, and a reminder before a booked time. Each window can override each one.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Buyers get an email and a notice in the portal's notification bell, and manage their email under Notification Preferences.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Adult Animal Pickup</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>When you approve a buyer for an adult animal, the portal's Pickups page shows the animal, the breeder, a status (Not yet ready, Ready, Scheduled, or Completed), and the pickup time once it is set.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>When the status is Ready, the buyer picks from the windows you set. A shared checklist shows which items are yours, which are the buyer's, and which are both.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="mr-3">•</span>
              <span>Once the pickup is scheduled, the buyer can download a transfer packet to keep offline.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 6: How BreederHQ Supports This -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4 bg-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] text-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">How BreederHQ brings it all together</h2>

      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed mb-8">
        When you give a client access, they get their own portal. Pedigrees, health records, contracts, photos, and payment history, all accessible 24/7. Built-in messaging keeps communication organized. You upload once, and they can access it anytime.
      </p>

      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Buyers get the information they need on their own schedule. You keep more of your day focused on the animals.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
        <a href="/pricing" class="inline-block bg-white text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] px-8 py-4 rounded-lg font-bold text-lg hover:bg-gray-100 transition text-center" style="min-height: 44px;">
          Join The Waitlist
        </a>
        <a href="/workflows/client-management" class="inline-block bg-transparent border-2 border-white text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-lg font-bold text-lg hover:bg-white hover:text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] transition text-center" style="min-height: 44px;">
          See client management →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 7: Who This Is For -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">Built for breeders who:</h2>

      <ul class="space-y-3 text-lg text-gray-700">
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>Field repetitive requests for documents and updates</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>Want to provide professional, always-available service</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>Track payments and need clients to see their balance</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>Share photos and updates without endless texting</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>Value their time and want to reduce interruptions</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="mr-3">•</span>
          <span>Manage more than a few clients at a time</span>
